# Copy this file to .env.local and edit it. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Nothing here is required: with every value unset the portal runs against its
# own bundled Node demo backend and needs no configuration at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which backend the UI talks to
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset (the default)
#   The UI calls its own /api/* route handlers, which are the Node demo backend
#   in demo-backend/. Just run `npm run dev`.
#
# Set to a URL
#   The UI calls that server instead, and demo-backend/ plus app/api/ go unused.
#   Every endpoint it must implement is written down in API-CONTRACT.md.
#
# To use the Java backend in java_backend/ (see java_backend/README.md):
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
#
# Use the SAME hostname the front end runs on. `npm run dev` serves 127.0.0.1,
# so pair it with 127.0.0.1 here. Cookies are shared across ports on one host,
# but 127.0.0.1 and localhost count as different hosts, and mixing them signs
# you out on every request.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Turnstile site key for the public account-deletion form. Leave it
# empty and the captcha is skipped entirely.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
